  nonce: e0f6  # e0f6
  message: "PRE-REGISTRATION 2026-09-07 (verbatim copy of ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/fasap_dbquery_09072026/PLAN.md, written before any subject-arm number exists):\n\n# WI-fasap — lazy Django QuerySet combinators leave the minting boundary (pre-registration)\n\nWritten 2026-09-07 BEFORE any subject-arm number exists. Baseline = measurement 0013's arm B ledger\n(`../mumov_qschain_09062026/B/`): `git diff --stat ddb9a02404 ac37d556bf -- packages/` is EMPTY, so dev's\nruntime files are the ones that ledger ran on. One subject arm on the branch; kserve as the control.\n\n## Two premises of the filed item that the tree refutes\n1. The Django rows are NOT in `io_primitives/python.yaml`; they are in the default overlay\n   `io_primitives_overlays/python-web-and-orm.yaml` (ADR-0047 ruling 1). Same effect on AUTO_SOURCE_LABEL_MAP.\n2. There is NO SQLAlchemy row and NO Ecto row anywhere (elixir.yaml: \"NO ELIXIR-OWN db_read / db_write ROWS\";\n   the F3 sweep already removed the nine `Ecto.Query` combinators). \"Parity\" there is moot. The other LAZY\n   members of ADR-0049's family (0009's table: java/kotlin/scala `TypedQuery.getResultStream`,\n   `EntityManager.getReference`, `sqlite3.Connection.iterdump`, the objc/swift NSURLSession task rows) are\n   OUT OF SCOPE here and FILED, because ruling 3 wants a represented-crossing proof per removal and the\n   Django licence (0013) does not transfer to them.\n\n## The F3 objection is live and decides the design\n`test_inv_nular_false_sources.py` keeps Django's lazy rows because \"the execution is an IMPLICIT `__iter__`\nwith NO CALL SITE TO CATALOGUE\". 0013's licence argument (executing reads are represented on the chain)\ncovers `get/first/exists/count/...` and NOT iteration. Pre-estimate from the baseline ledger\n(`preestimate.py`, `shape_scan.py`): 62 of pretix's 139 situations rest ONLY on lazy sources; a text heuristic\nclasses 28 as write-receiver-only (`X.objects.filter(...).delete()` — the vacuous L class), 12 as EVALUATED\nIN SCOPE (`for op in qs:`, `list(X.objects.filter(...))`, `for i in qs[:n]`), 2 both, 20 unclear.\nSo a retag alone deletes real in-scope reads — the 0010 HANDLE precedent (\"retagging would delete a true,\nuseful finding ... catalogue the reads first\"). Ruling 3's two halves therefore land in ONE change:\n\n## Design\nA. **`db_compose`** — a deferred_crossing registry value (`io_boundary_types.py`): inbound, catalogue-declarable,\n   NOT in the headline, absent from AUTO_SOURCE_LABEL_MAP, shadowing `db_read` via DEFERRED_CROSSING_SHADOWS.\n   Envelope key `db_compose_edges`; IO_BOUNDARIES_SCHEMA_VERSION 2.2 -> 2.3; filtered CLI path in step.\n   NOT named `db_query`: that string is already the database_query linker's `call_kind` value and means\n   \"a call that EXECUTES a query\" — the opposite reading.\nB. **Overlay retag**: the 21 QuerySet-returning members (exactly `library_signatures/python.yaml`'s\n   django.db.models rows — a parity test pins lazy <=> type-preserving, dunders excluded) move to\n   `db_compose`. Executing reads stay `db_read`: get first last count exists aggregate earliest latest\n   in_bulk iterator, PLUS two new rows `__iter__` and `__getitem__` (the evaluation call sites).\nC. **py.py evaluation call sites** (ruling 3's first half): a `calls` edge to `django.db.models.__iter__`\n   at `for`/`async for`/comprehension iter, and at `list|tuple|set|frozenset|sorted|dict|enumerate(<qs>)`\n   (first positional arg, builtin name not rebound in scope); `django.db.models.__getitem__` at an INDEX\n   subscript; a SLICE subscript propagates the type (signature row `django.db.models.__getitem__`).\n   meta: call_construct=\"protocol\", framework_dispatch=\"django_orm\", resolution_quality=\"type_inferred\".\n   NOT represented (stated, filed as residual): `__len__`/`__bool__` (scalar, the 0001 branch-condition\n   shape; `count()`/`exists()` carry it where spelled), `yield from`, starred, a QuerySet handed to another\n   scope (`return qs`, form `queryset=`, `Paginator(qs)`) — those are the DEFERRED class the shadow discloses.\nD. Docs: ADR-0049 implementation state (in place), ADR-0050 sections table + \"nineteen\" -> twenty, registry\n   docstring, spec vocabulary line + envelope, concept-axes, CHANGELOG, measurement 0014 (+ README row).\n\n## Pre-registered predictions (pretix subject arm vs the 0013-B baseline; kserve control)\nP1  0013's own control: the 28 L situations VANISH; the 7 R-TP situations REMAIN (keyed (claim, source fn)).\nP2  Of the 62 lazy-only baseline situations: the 28 write-receiver-only VANISH; the 12 evaluated-in-scope\n    SURVIVE via `__iter__`/`__getitem__`; the 2 BOTH survive; the 20 unclear are read and classed.\nP3  kserve: 0 moved. No verdict category moves in either repo (every affected claim already `violated`).\nP4  New situations appear only where an evaluation site exists in a function that had NO lazy source before\n    (e.g. a QuerySet parameter is NOT typed, so `list(queryset.filter(q))` adds nothing). Expected small; every\n    NEW situation is read back too.\nRefutation / ship rule: EVERY vanished situation is read at source and classed L (write-receiver, vacuous),\nI (evaluated in scope — a DECLARED shape of C missed = a bug, fix before merge), X (evaluated by a shape\noutside C's declared set — counted as the cost, filed, PR still ships), D (handed to another scope — the\ndeferred class, correctly disclosed). If any I-class vanished situation is TP+useful under 0001/ADR-0046,\nthe PR does not merge until C catches it.\nINV-buzab three-row check: tagged+shadowed -> `confirmed_with_caveats` naming the site; shadow emptied ->\nbare `confirmed` (the false all-clear the design refuses, pinned as the costly control); fs_write untouched.\nAwaits_bakeoff_validation on merge."  # e0f6
